  "question": {
    "text": "$\\quad$ If $\\cos 7 \\theta=\\cos \\theta-\\sin 4 \\theta,$ then the general value\r\n\r\nof $\\theta$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{n \\pi}{6}, \\frac{n \\pi}{3}+(-1)^{n} \\frac{\\pi}{18}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{n \\pi}{3}, \\frac{n \\pi}{3}+(-1)^{n} \\frac{\\pi}{18}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{n \\pi}{4}, \\frac{n \\pi}{3} \\pm \\frac{\\pi}{18}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{n \\pi}{4}, \\frac{n \\pi}{3}+(-1)^{n} \\frac{\\pi}{18}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\cos 7 \\theta=\\cos \\theta-\\sin 4 \\theta$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\sin 4 \\theta=\\cos \\theta-\\cos 7 \\theta$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\sin 4 \\theta=2 \\sin 4 \\theta \\sin 3 \\theta$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\sin 4 \\theta(1-2 \\sin 3 \\theta)=0$\r\n\r\n$\\therefore \\sin 4 \\theta=0$ or $\\sin 3 \\theta=\\frac{1}{2}$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow 4 \\theta=n \\pi$ or $3 \\theta=n \\pi+(-1)^{n} \\frac{\\pi}{6}$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad \\theta=\\frac{n \\pi}{4}$ or $\\frac{n \\pi}{3}+(-1)^{n} \\frac{\\pi}{18}$"
  }
}